  "verbalization": "Stavudine, a nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor, is linked to Slc22a6 through a shared biological pathway involving nucleoside analogs. The evidence suggests that Stavudine, Didanosine, and Zidovudine, all classified as nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors, bind to Slc22a6. This binding is consistent across multiple paths, with the lowest common ancestor of Stavudine and its analogs being the organic heteromonocyclic compound, which further links them to the nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor category. The mechanism appears to involve the interaction of these compounds with Slc22a6, likely through a common molecular interaction that is not explicitly detailed in the provided evidence. The relationship between Stavudine and Slc22a6 is thus supported by the collective evidence of their shared binding to the same transporter, reinforcing a role in the transport of these nucleoside analogs across cellular membranes.",
